module gunbc.plans.ci_merge_freshness

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetirement, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { p }
import gunbc.design_ruling { project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts }

fn ci_merge_freshness_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "Goal: prevent stale-green merges. A PR validated before a newer gate or consumer lands can merge a broken combined tree despite green checks and approvals. Require validation of the merge-result against current main; another lens cannot supply freshness."),
    p(text: "Historical receipts: #5429 head f66c26b1 passed before gate #5418, then merged unchanged and broke main until #5465; #5445/#5453 share the class. Existing realization_vocab.clean_tree_test and external_authority.live_anchored_modules_clean_test provide non-vacuous forward coverage only at the tested base. Reverse-staleness roster soundness (#5466 mode) separately catches dead anchors/excuses; it does not repair freshness."),
    p(text: "3. Operator decision remains: prefer merge queue, which tests current-main composition without author resync/approval churn; alternatively require-up-to-date branches plus required floor checks. Either is a repo-admin/merge-policy change. Queue adoption replaces manual parallel merges; up-to-date policy retains them but restales head-keyed approvals after resync. Historical traffic/provider-outage figures explain the recommendation, not current conditions."),
    p(text: "ci_failure_class.floor_exit_blocks_merge computes and surfaces success/unambiguous-Infra nonblocking versus Structural blocking; a lone exit-137 is Structural, not guessed infrastructure. #5651 re-landed after #5627 reverted #5615, on #5640’s TestClaim→AssertionClaim de-fork. This is executed-visible evidence, not live enforcement: no merge consumer currently follows from that receipt. Never wire the verdict into CI-floor host exit semantics; repeated OOM→block→rerun can livelock."),
    p(text: "Enforcement prerequisites BOTH: cross-run reclassification must recognize clustered simultaneous deaths/host-uptime resets instead of treating a lone exit as proof; cap recovery (#5650/operator oomd in the dated plan) must restore session slack before reruns add load. Only the operator’s freshness mechanism consumes the verdict after those prerequisites. The unwired interim retires with that witnessed consumption, not a self-asserted flag."),
    p(text: "Further receipt, 2026-09-10: #10933 added fabric_m0_publication_witness using DurableOriginRead/DisposableCacheRead while #10934 deleted those carriers. #10934’s successful run 34520652774 started before #10933 merged and never saw it; its unchanged df47e1d7670 head merged at a4b21cb8e47. Run 34531957010 found the pair’s two missing imports; unrelated grain_admits_single_cabinet was a third finding, repaired by #10968. #10977/38fde6682a8 repaired this pair. Source inspection also found obsolete ReadbackConfirmed/ManifestRead fields, not findings of the declarations run that stopped earlier. Text conflict review and one manager knowing both lanes did not validate composition."),
    p(text: "Validation: no PR may merge when its last-tested base predates current main, with freshness established by execution over the composed tree. This capability was never held; its absence is the Plan retirement obligation, not a rung-drop regression from an achieved guarantee."),
  ]
}

data ci_merge_freshness_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly { ruling: project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts },
  slug: "ci-merge-freshness",
  title: "CI merge-freshness — decision record (the stale-green root of the 3× fleet-red)",
  body: ci_merge_freshness_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Delete this doc when the merge-time freshness requirement of §3 is in force as a witnessed property — a merge-queue (Option 1) or require-up-to-date required-check (Option 2) is wired so that no PR can merge while last-validated against a base that pre-dates current `main` — at which point stale-green is unwritable by construction and this decision record is redundant.")
  }
}
